onent and I thought is he trying to  trick me  because if I play tonight captures any  fun he has this Queen to e7 move and  well then white doesn't really I mean  white is still better of course but he  does have to play a game because Knight  Queen to h5 trick doesn't work here  because after g6 you don't have this  Knight captures and g6 option because  Queen captures on e4 with Czech and  after Bishop to e2 Queen captures  tonight on g6 white is down a piece and  black is winning this game but after  this f6 move I did capture the pawn on  e5 as I I thought now he doesn't know  anything about chess he doesn't know  what the damiano defenses and well the  most famous famous occurrence of this  opening was actually in 1964 mr. Robert  MacGregor actually played this f6 idea  against Bobby Fischer as Fischer was  holding a simultaneous exhibition and  well Fischer did play Knight captures on  e5 and he got this response Queen to e7  and the Robert MacGregor was able to  drew the draw a game against the Bobby  Fischer so in this game I played Knight  captures an e5 but of course my opponent  did not play Queen to e7 he played F  captures on e5 I played Queen to h5  check he didn't put g6 he played King to  e7 and well at this point I knew that my  opponent wasn't really a good chess  player so I went Queen captures any five  check he went King to seven Bishop to c4  check now he didn't even push d5 plating  to g6 and well Queen to a5 check King to  h6 now d4 opening a discover check from  the bishop and c1 we have G 5 here I  pushed h4 and after Bishop to e7 I just  captured it's an it's check from the  pawn and from the rook on h1 King to g7  and Queen to f7 and this is checkmate so  ok my opponents congratulated me and  well I refuse to take his money because  it was a the game was too easy I mean to  take someone $20 but then actually he  insisted we play another game and I  thought well why do you want to play  another game I mean you just lost the  game in like 